1
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:04,800
Hi. I'm Malcolm Stewart.

2
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:06,100
John Marchetta.

3
00:00:06,100 --> 00:00:09,700
Sit down, sit down.

4
00:00:09,700 --> 00:00:12,600
Susan has told me a great deal about you.

5
00:00:12,600 --> 00:00:14,500
She says you're quite a man.

6
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:14,700
She says

7
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:18,400
a lot of wonderful things about you too, Mr. Stewart.

8
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:20,600
That's always nice to hear, Mr. Marchetta.

9
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:22,300
Call me John.

10
00:00:22,300 --> 00:00:24,800
May I call you Malcolm?

11
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:26,500
Let's talk business.

12
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:28,300
That's music to my ears.

13
00:00:28,300 --> 00:00:28,700
I understand

14
00:00:28,700 --> 00:00:31,200
you used to be in the construction business.

15
00:00:31,200 --> 00:00:34,300
Yup. Forty-three years.

16
00:00:34,300 --> 00:00:35,900
Here's a brief description

17
00:00:35,900 --> 00:00:42,500
of forty-three years of on-the-job training.

18
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:45,300
That is some history!

19
00:00:45,300 --> 00:00:47,300
You're a valuable asset, Malcolm.

20
00:00:47,300 --> 00:00:49,200
Very valuable.

21
00:00:49,200 --> 00:00:51,300
Thank you.

22
00:00:51,300 --> 00:00:54,900
Yup. Forty-three years.

23
00:00:54,900 --> 00:00:57,273
Half that time in my own construction company.

24
00:00:57,273 --> 00:01:01,035
Big jobs--factories, shopping malls.

25
00:01:01,035 --> 00:01:02,877
That kind of thing.

26
00:01:02,877 --> 00:01:04,000
Then you retired.

27
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:05,700
Yes.

28
00:01:05,700 --> 00:01:07,900
After my wife died,

29
00:01:07,900 --> 00:01:09,700
and I felt I should spend more time

30
00:01:09,700 --> 00:01:12,925
with my children and grandchildren.

31
00:01:12,925 --> 00:01:14,400
I lived in Florida,

32
00:01:14,400 --> 00:01:15,800
and they lived in New York.

33
00:01:15,800 --> 00:01:16,796
I understand.

34
00:01:16,796 --> 00:01:19,113
My dautghter Cami lives in New York.

35
00:01:19,113 --> 00:01:21,400
I like being near her.

36
00:01:21,400 --> 00:01:22,875
When I came here,

37
00:01:22,875 --> 00:01:25,500
I planned to take a few months off.

38
00:01:25,500 --> 00:01:30,400
Relax with the family and then look for some work.

39
00:01:30,400 --> 00:01:32,800
Put my experience on the line ...

40
00:01:32,800 --> 00:01:34,800
but, unfortunately,

41
00:01:34,800 --> 00:01:37,200
there isn't any work for a retired person my age.

42
00:01:37,200 --> 00:01:38,300
Sometimes there is,

43
00:01:38,300 --> 00:01:41,000
and sometimes there isn't.

44
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:42,635
Well, I'm involved with an organization,

45
00:01:42,635 --> 00:01:45,800
and we're trying to resolve that problem.

46
00:01:45,800 --> 00:01:47,000
What's that?

47
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:48,800
TOPS.

48
00:01:48,800 --> 00:01:54,900
T-O-P-S--means Talented Older People's Society.

49
00:01:54,900 --> 00:01:57,100
I'd like to be a member.

50
00:01:57,100 --> 00:01:57,900
How much are the dues?

51
00:01:57,900 --> 00:02:00,800
There are no dues.

52
00:02:00,800 --> 00:02:03,500
The organization serves major companies in this city.

53
00:02:03,500 --> 00:02:05,200
Why?

54
00:02:05,200 --> 00:02:07,722
Because our members are men and women like you.

55
00:02:07,722 --> 00:02:11,900
Experienced, talented, retired.

56
00:02:11,900 --> 00:02:13,700
But our members want to go out there

57
00:02:13,700 --> 00:02:14,800
and use their talents.

58
00:02:14,800 --> 00:02:17,600
They want to work.

59
00:02:17,600 --> 00:02:19,400
That is fantastic, John!

60
00:02:19,400 --> 00:02:23,611
I've got an idea for you, Malcolm.

61
00:02:23,611 --> 00:02:25,076
Just fill out this form for me.

62
00:02:25,076 --> 00:02:27,000
It'll only take a few minutes.

63
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:27,600
Sit right here,

64
00:02:27,600 --> 00:02:29,630
and do it while I talk to my secretary.

65
00:02:29,630 --> 00:02:33,100
When I get back, we'll talk about my new factory.

66
00:02:33,100 --> 00:02:34,818
My company is a member of TOPS.

67
00:02:34,818 --> 00:02:38,300
So I try hard to find opportunities for people like you.

68
00:02:38,300 --> 00:02:39,887
Malcolm.

69
00:02:39,887 --> 00:02:41,000
And when I see an opportunity,

70
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:43,500
I can act on it.

71
00:02:43,500 --> 00:02:49,300
Well, I can use your brainpower on the job right now.

72
00:02:49,300 --> 00:02:50,000
Have you got time this morning

73
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:53,000
to go over to the construction site with me?

74
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:54,800
I'd like to have you meet my foreman--

75
00:02:54,800 --> 00:02:56,700
get some background on the job.

76
00:02:56,700 --> 00:02:59,100
I've got plenty of time.

77
00:02:59,100 --> 00:03:00,400
I'll be right back.

78
00:03:00,400 --> 00:03:19,942
We'll go over to the job site together.

79
00:03:19,942 --> 00:03:24,199
Malcolm, you worked on the Spaceport project?

80
00:03:24,199 --> 00:03:27,318
My company was the contractor.

81
00:03:27,318 --> 00:03:29,535
I built the theater there

82
00:03:29,535 --> 00:03:31,347
with my own two hands, practically.

83
00:03:31,347 --> 00:03:32,238
I understand.

84
00:03:32,238 --> 00:03:32,604
Well,

85
00:03:32,604 --> 00:03:35,634
I'm glad to see you two guys getting along so well

86
00:03:35,634 --> 00:03:36,980
because, Danny,

87
00:03:36,980 --> 00:03:38,099
Malcolm is on the TOPS team.

88
00:03:38,099 --> 00:03:40,604
He's going to be working with you for a while.

89
00:03:40,604 --> 00:03:43,544
His experience will be valuable to both of us.

90
00:03:43,544 --> 00:03:45,276
Welcome aboard, Malcolm!

91
00:03:45,276 --> 00:03:47,200
I'm going back to my office.

92
00:03:47,200 --> 00:03:48,108
Give me a call later, Malcolm.

93
00:03:48,108 --> 00:03:51,147
I'll tell you the time and date of the next TOPS meeting.

94
00:03:51,147 --> 00:03:51,900
I'd like you to meet the group.

95
00:03:51,900 --> 00:03:53,513
I will, John.

96
00:03:53,513 --> 00:03:54,800
And again--thanks.

97
00:03:54,800 --> 00:03:57,800
No ... thank you.

98
00:03:57,800 --> 00:04:01,631
And thank Susan.

99
00:04:01,631 --> 00:04:03,400
He's quite a man.

100
00:04:03,400 --> 00:04:06,200
A real inspiration for me.

101
00:04:06,200 --> 00:04:08,900
[04:07.02]OK, Danny.

102
00:04:08,900 --> 00:04:09,300
I know you didn't expect to have me around,

103
00:04:09,300 --> 00:04:11,808
but I think I can be of some help to you.

104
00:04:11,808 --> 00:04:13,200
Let me tell you something, Malcolm.

105
00:04:13,200 --> 00:04:14,700
With your background and experience,

106
00:04:14,700 --> 00:04:15,800
I can learn something

107
00:04:15,800 --> 00:04:17,700
... and I do need some advice on a difficult problem.

108
00:04:17,700 --> 00:04:22,768
Let me show you this.

109
00:04:22,768 --> 00:04:26,100
I don't want to give you a final opinion

110
00:04:26,100 --> 00:04:30,100
without studying these building plans more carefully.

111
00:04:30,100 --> 00:04:33,658
But a simple solution might be

112
00:04:33,658 --> 00:04:35,600
to move the air-conditioning units

113
00:04:35,600 --> 00:04:38,700
instead of redesigning the entire system.

114
00:04:38,700 --> 00:04:42,500
It might be simpler and less expensive .

115
00:04:42,500 --> 00:04:46,200
You just earned your weight in gold, Malcolm.

116
00:04:46,200 --> 00:04:50,597
Welcome aboard!

117
00:04:50,597 --> 00:04:53,100
It all happened so quickly!

118
00:04:53,100 --> 00:04:54,400
I can't believe it!

119
00:04:54,400 --> 00:04:56,715
I'm glad Mr. Marchetta was so helpful.

120
00:04:56,715 --> 00:04:57,800
He was more than helpful.

121
00:04:57,800 --> 00:05:01,300
He actually took me to meet his foreman.

122
00:05:01,300 --> 00:05:03,900
I'm thrilled for you, Grandpa.

123
00:05:03,900 --> 00:05:07,090
I don't know how to thank you, Susan.

124
00:05:07,090 --> 00:05:09,500
You're a wonderful granddaughter.

125
00:05:09,500 --> 00:05:11,387
It's good to see you so happy.

126
00:05:11,387 --> 00:05:13,921
I'll be at the construction site tomorrow.

127
00:05:13,921 --> 00:05:15,100
What are you doing tomorrow night?

128
00:05:15,100 --> 00:05:16,376
I'm not doing anything.

129
00:05:16,376 --> 00:05:17,802
Why?

130
00:05:17,802 --> 00:05:20,000
How about a date with your grandfather?

131
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:22,600
I owe you a good steak dinner.

132
00:05:22,600 --> 00:05:24,500
I'll accept.

133
00:05:24,500 --> 00:05:24,800
Tomorrow night.

134
00:05:24,800 --> 00:05:26,969
You and me. Dinner.

135
00:05:26,969 --> 00:05:28,200
What time?

136
00:05:28,200 --> 00:05:30,395
I'll pick you up here at seven .

137
00:05:30,395 --> 00:05:31,600
Is that OK?

138
00:05:31,600 --> 00:05:32,400
I can't wait!

139
00:05:32,400 --> 00:05:33,800
And you can tell me

140
00:05:33,800 --> 00:05:36,800
all about your first full day back on the job.

141
00:05:36,800 --> 00:05:39,800
It's a deal!
